course: dictionary
lesson: 8080
title: Short words with long meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are shortened. «REM sleep, short for rapid eye movement, is when most vivid dreams happen.» The words «short for» tell you that REM is a short form of a longer name. Capital letters often mean an abbreviation, so REM is written in capitals.
explain: The small word «rem» on its own is different. Context clues help here: a science lesson about radiation and harm to the body tells you it is a unit of measurement, not a stage of sleep.
explain: Always check the words around the word. Swap your meaning into the sentence. If «REM sleep» becomes «rapid eye movement sleep», it still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: REM stands for «rapid eye movement», a stage of sleep when your eyes move quickly under your eyelids.
fact: Most vivid dreams happen in REM sleep, and everyone dreams several times a night, even if they forget.
fact: A rem is an old unit for measuring how much radiation a body has taken in; scientists now use the sievert.
fact: «rem» is also a piece of longer words, such as «remember».
exercise: «REM sleep, short for rapid eye movement, is when most vivid dreams happen.» What does REM stand for? | Rest, eat, move | Remember every memory | Really excellent mood | *Rapid eye movement
exercise: During REM sleep, what happens to your eyes? | They stay still and wide open | *They move quickly under your eyelids | They glow in the dark | They close and never move again
exercise: Which longer word contains the letters «rem»? | river | *remember | sunshine | castle
test: «Babies spend about half their sleep in REM, grown-ups only about a fifth.» What does this tell you? | *Babies spend more of their sleep in REM than grown-ups do | Babies never dream | Grown-ups never sleep | Grown-ups spend more of their sleep in REM than babies
test: Scientists now use the sievert, but the old unit for radiation was the «rem». What did the rem measure? | How many dreams you have in a night | How fast your eyes move in sleep | *How much radiation a body has taken in | How long a night's sleep lasts
exam: «The brain switches off most muscles in REM sleep so you do not act out your dreams.» Why does this happen? | So your eyes can close tightly | *So you do not act out your dreams | So you can remember your dreams perfectly | So you can wake up faster
